  "unresolved": [],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "f1-markdownlint-no-column",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/runtime/cleanup.mjs:548",
      "summary": "markdownlint-cli2 prints \"file:line rule ...\" (no colon after the line) for rules with no column, such as MD041. checkLine needs \"path:line:\", so those lines are dropped silently when the same run has another matching line (probe: 1 of 2 problems found). The template example uses markdownlint-cli2, so a user who copies it gets partial findings.",
      "assumption": "The spec contract is \"path:line: message\"; accepting \"path:line \" too is a widening for the owner."
    },
    {
      "id": "f2-knip-needs-wrapper",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/references/setup.md:308",
      "summary": "setup.md offers knip, but no knip reporter prints path:line: at the line start (the default symbols reporter puts it in the third column). A knip entry gives only the fallback \"failed with no path:line: output\" finding. A vale entry needs --output=line. So drift/docaudit (if they print the line contract) plug in with only a joycraft.yaml entry; vale and markdownlint need the right flag; knip needs a wrapper script. settings.md and the template do not say to pick a line output format."
    },
    {
      "id": "f3-absolute-paths",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/runtime/cleanup.mjs:570",
      "summary": "A tool that prints absolute paths (eslint unix formatter) gives findings with the absolute path; it is not made relative to the project root, so context-first ranking and path matching do not apply to it."
    },
    {
      "id": "f4-space-in-path",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/runtime/cleanup.mjs:548",
      "summary": "A path with a space (\"docs/my notes.md:2: bad\") does not match checkLine (by design, to exclude stack traces), so it gives only the fallback finding."
    },
    {
      "id": "f5-pipeline-not-found",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/runtime/cleanup.mjs:564",
      "summary": "run: \"definitely-not-a-tool-xyz | cat\" exits 0 through the shell pipeline, so it is neither skipped nor reported; the missing tool is silent."
    },
    {
      "id": "f6-subdir-cwd",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/runtime/cleanup.mjs:582",
      "summary": "tidy uses process.cwd() as root; run from a subdirectory it reads no joycraft.yaml, so no checks run and nothing says so (probe \"run from a subdirectory\"). Shared with the other tidy checks, not specific to this spec."
    },
    {
      "id": "f7-column-in-detail",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/runtime/cleanup.mjs:570",
      "summary": "For path:line:col: tools (vale line, eslint unix, markdownlint with a column) the column stays at the start of detail (\"5:Vale.Spelling:...\"). Cosmetic."
    },
    {
